INT. SELF-STORAGE FACILITY, UNIT 214 - NIGHT

A concrete corridor lined with orange roll-up doors. A buzzing fluorescent tube. A single padlock hangs open.

MERCER, 40s, in a black windbreaker, hauls up the door of unit 214. LINN, 30s, her partner, in a hooded parka, holds a flashlight. OTTO, 60s, a gaunt night manager in a security fleece, stands behind them, jangling keys. SABA, 20s, a rental clerk, hangs back at the corner with her phone raised.

Inside the unit: a card table, one folding chair, and a wall of photographs pinned and strung with red thread.

                    LINN
          Jesus.

                    MERCER
          That's his handwriting.

                    OTTO
          I told them it was rented to an accountant.

                    SABA
          I'm recording this, by the way.

                    MERCER
          Delete it.

                    SABA
          ^It's for my own protection.

                    OTTO
          ^Let her.

Mercer sighs and steps into the unit. Linn follows with the beam.
